 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489181 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1458db49-4a48-5b8a-8849-91c1b7ef8d88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489181 #edb/ref 1074 "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-2,0,1,2\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/579e17e56674e39e552f1c0856f40e7f878ed94248a7a0e878c1f851c54ecbea.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ecf9c80-3378-55e5-9ee3-61d34805f6d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489217 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-3.$ This occurs at the point $(3,-3).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs at the point $(-1,1).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-3$ and $1,$ including both $-3$ and $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-3\\le y\\le 1,$ which can also be written as  $-3\\le f(x)\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
